raction exactly once ΓÇö the sum of the costs of the tour roads is independent of the tour. Volodya is curious if you can find such price system with all road prices not greater than 1000.\n\n## Input\n\nInput contains just one natural number ( 3ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë N ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë20 ) ΓÇö the number of town attractions.\n\n## Output\n\nOutput should contain N rows containing N positive integer numbers each ΓÇö the adjacency matrix of the prices graph (thus, j -th number in i -th row should be equal to the price of the road between the j -th and the i -th attraction). Diagonal numbers should be equal to zero. All numbers should not be greater than 1000. All prices should be positive and pairwise distinct. If there are several solutions, output any of them.\n\n## Examples\n\nExample 1:\n```\n3\n```\n```\n0 3 4 \n3 0 5 \n4 5 0\n```","type":"text"}],"contestId":42,"index":"D","memoryLimit":"256 megabytes","name":"Strange town","problemKey":"42-D","rating":null,"tags":[],"timeLimit":"2 seconds","url":"https://codeforces.com/contest/42/problem/D"},{"approaches":[{"label":"Approach 1","number":1,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 2","number":2,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 3","number":3,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 4","number":4,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 5","number":5,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 6","number":6,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 7","number":7,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 8","number":8,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 9","number":9,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 10","number":10,"solutions":[{"